### nix-init
.direnv
.pre-commit-config.yaml

# The root layer deliberately has NO committed lock. Its flake.nix pins every
# input to an exact commit, so a lock adds a second copy of the same fact that
# can disagree with the first. Nix writes this file whenever the flake is
# evaluated, and `git add` picks it up, so it is ignored rather than merely
# absent: without this line the next edit to flake.nix commits a lock by
# accident, and nothing would notice.
flake.lock
